\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces Observational decision thresholds on the measured local-template $f_{\rm  NL}$ (horizontal axis). Shaded regions, left to right: dark green --- measurement near the $-35/8$ prediction, strongly favors the bounce; light green --- negative $f_{\rm  NL}$ of bounce-compatible magnitude, supports the bounce; dark red (legend label ``bounce excluded'') --- measurement consistent with zero, disfavoring the quasi-dust matter bounce while remaining consistent with standard single-field inflation; light red --- positive $f_{\rm  NL}$, disfavoring the bounce and instead supporting exotic multifield inflation. Blue vertical line: bounce prediction $f_{\rm  NL}= -35/8$; black dotted line: standard inflation $f_{\rm  NL}\approx 0$. Error bars: SPHEREx ($\sigma = 0.7$) and MegaMapper conservative ($\sigma = 1.5$), both centered on the bounce prediction.}}{22}{figure.6}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:thresholds}{{6}{22}{Observational decision thresholds on the measured local-template $\fnl $ (horizontal axis). Shaded regions, left to right: dark green --- measurement near the $-35/8$ prediction, strongly favors the bounce; light green --- negative $\fnl $ of bounce-compatible magnitude, supports the bounce; dark red (legend label ``bounce excluded'') --- measurement consistent with zero, disfavoring the quasi-dust matter bounce while remaining consistent with standard single-field inflation; light red --- positive $\fnl $, disfavoring the bounce and instead supporting exotic multifield inflation. Blue vertical line: bounce prediction $\fnl = -35/8$; black dotted line: standard inflation $\fnl \approx 0$. Error bars: SPHEREx ($\sigma = 0.7$) and MegaMapper conservative ($\sigma = 1.5$), both centered on the bounce prediction}{figure.6}{}}
