\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {V}{\ignorespaces Sensitivity of the SPHEREx detection significance to single- vs full-time-ordering in the matter-bounce $f_{\rm  NL}$ derivation. Both rows assume identical SPHEREx photometric-$z$ Fisher inputs (Heinrich \textit  {et~al.}~\cite  {Heinrich:2023}) with $\sigma (f_{\rm  NL})=0.7$ in the bispectrum channel and the noise-weighted template overlap $r=0.84$ from Sec.~\ref {sec:template}; the only difference is which $|f_{\rm  NL}|$ value is used to compute the significance $|f_{\rm  NL}|\,r/\sigma (f_{\rm  NL})$. The Cai row is the physical bispectrum (full in-in commutator, $-2\,\mathrm  {Im}$ identity); the Li row is the single-time-ordering intermediate and is shown only as a robustness check on the operator-algebra step, not as an alternative physical normalization.}}{28}{table.5}\protected@file@percent }
